notes: 'NBRC1463 uses5g dry yeast and separately0.1g yeast extract; NBRC828 uses10g
  dry yeast. The material category is dried yeast biomass, distinct from extract.
  Species, viability, particle size, manufacturer and drying process are unknown;
  two contexts share only this generic material scope, not a proven product or lot.
  FOODON dry-yeast search found more specific torula/brewer and fine/active/inactive
  terms whose additional qualifiers are unsupported. Raw labels retained as occurrence
  provenance only: [''Dry yeast'']. Identity is the stated physical material, not
  an arbitrary recipe-specific duplicate. Existing generic yeast, baker yeast and
  wet cell paste do not establish this supplied state.'
